# A 360 KB diskette moved from B into A (roadmap disk-scheduler.md M8, D12,
# D13): tests/posix/media.c (TEST_MEDIA_MOVEB) on MAME, whose Lua takes both
# diskettes out and puts B's into A (media-at:). A's change line says so, the
# driver finds the diskette at 300 kbit/s, 360 KB in a 1.2 MB drive, and
# Read ID on its second track says whether to step twice (MAME's tracks are
# a cylinder each, an AT's 48-tpi diskette's two); B's file is read there,
# and the volume is read-only in A.
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_MEDIA
define: TEST_MEDIA_MOVEB
emulators: mame
media-at: 75 eject A
media-at: 75 eject B
media-at: 77 insert A b
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
match: contains
timeout: 600
---
media: B's readme.txt (bytes): {...}
media: A's readme.txt, B's diskette (bytes): {...}
media: a write there (EROFS 30): 30
media: done
